meta {
  name: 1 - Tenant A Token On Tenant B Host
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenant/branding
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Host: {{tenantBHost}}
  X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantAId}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{tenantAAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns expected status", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus() === 403 || res.getStatus() === 500).to.equal(true);
  });
}

docs {
  X-Tenant-Id is sent to prove it is ignored -- Host + JWT are the only authority.

  KNOWN BUG (found by running this collection against a live local instance on 2026-07-20):
  the docs/http harness say this should be 403 with errors[0].code == TENANT_MISMATCH, but the
  live app currently returns a bare 500 (Spring Boot's default /error page, no JSON envelope).
  Root cause: TenantContextFilter throws TenantMismatchException from a plain servlet Filter
  positioned before DispatcherServlet even runs, so GlobalExceptionHandler's @ExceptionHandler
  (which maps it to 403) never gets a chance to run -- Spring Security's ExceptionTranslationFilter
  only translates AuthenticationException/AccessDeniedException, not this. Access is still denied
  (no branding data leaks), just with the wrong status/body. See TenantContextFilter.java:53 and
  GlobalExceptionHandler.java:90-94.
}
